title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.3, Revision 3

- Add enumerants for
  * SPV_KHR_vulkan_memory_model

- Fixed Issues:
  * Typo: say <<OpMatrixTimesVector, *OpMatrixTimesVector*>> is *Matrix* X *Vector*.
  * Update on Khronos SPIR-V issue #244: Added *Shader* and *Kernel* capabilities to the *2D* <<Dim, dimensionality>>.
  * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #317: Clarify that the *Uniform* <<Decoration, decoration>> should apply only to objects,
    and that the <<DynamicInstance, dynamic instance>> of the object is the same, rather than at the consumer usage.
  * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #335: Clarify and correct <<Validation, when it is valid>> for pointers to be operands to *OpFunctionCall*.
    Corrections are believed to be consistent with existing front-end and back-end support.
  * Khronos SPIR-V Issue #344: don't include inactive invocations in what makes the result of
    <<OpGroupNonUniformBallotBitExtract, *OpGroupNonUniformBallotBitExtract*>> undefined.
